WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.957
NumPy is excellent for homogeneous numerical arrays.

00:00:03.957 --> 00:00:11.962
Pandas builds on the same array-oriented thinking but adds labels, table structure, mixed data types,

00:00:11.962 --> 00:00:20.111
missing-data tools, joins, grouping operations, and convenient methods for real-world tabular analysis.

00:00:20.561 --> 00:00:27.578
The transition is natural. In NumPy, we think about positions, dimensions, and axes.

00:00:27.578 --> 00:00:36.438
In Pandas, we keep those ideas but also gain column names and indexes that make tables easier to interpret.

00:00:36.438 --> 00:00:44.823
The next module will focus on Pandas, where we will use these numerical foundations to work with more realistic datasets

00:00:44.823 --> 00:00:51.500
that contain numbers, text, dates, missing values, and multiple related tables.
